LatticePolytopes -- for computations with lattice polytopes
***********************************************************

Description
===========

A lattice polytope is a bounded object of the type *note Polyhedron:
(Polyhedra)Polyhedron,. This package is focused on functions that are specific
for lattice polytopes rather than general polyhedra. Examples of such methods
are *note isCayley: isCayley, , *note cayley: cayley, and *note randZPoly:
randZPoly,. Moreover the package contains known classifications of smooth
2-polytopes with up to 12 lattice points and smooth 3-polytopes with up to 16
lattice points. These classifications are accessible via the functions *note
listSmooth2D: listSmooth2D, and *note listSmooth3D: listSmooth3D,


LatticePolytopes uses the *note Polyhedra: (Polyhedra)Top, package by René
Birkner (see http://page.mi.fu-berlin.de/rbirkner/ ) and the *note
NormalToricVarieties: (NormalToricVarieties)Top, package by Gregory Smith (see
http://www.mast.queensu.ca/~ggsmith/ )


The following is an example illustrating the main functions provided in the
package.
  * *note Working with lattice polytopes: Working with lattice polytopes,


For an introduction to polytopes, we recommend Günter M. Ziegler's (see
http://www.math.tu-berlin.de/~ziegler/ ) Lectures on Polytopes, Graduate Texts
in Mathematics 152, Springer-Verlag, New York, 1995.

