adjointPolytope -- computes the adjoint of a polytope
*****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        adjointPolytope(X,k)
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note convex polyhedron: (Polyhedra)Polyhedron,,  or a a *note
        matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix, where the columns are the vertice points
      * k, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,,  an integer.
  * Outputs:
      * a *note convex polyhedron: (Polyhedra)Polyhedron,, The adjoint Polytope
        of X corresponding to the line bundle kK+L, see the article Polyhedral
        adjunction theory (see http://msp.org/ant/2013/7-10/p02.xhtml ) by
        Sandra Di Rocco, Christian Haase, Benjamin Nill and Andreas Paffenholz.

Description
===========


adjointPolytope is a function that compute the k:th adjoint of a polytope
+------------------------------------+
|i1 : adjointPolytope(hypercube(2),1)|
|                                    |
|o1 = Polyhedron{...1...}            |
|                                    |
|o1 : Polyhedron                     |
+------------------------------------+

