degreeOfJetSeparation -- computes the degree of jetSeparation at a given point
******************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        degreeOfJetSeparation(A,pt)
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,,  or  a *note list:
        (Macaulay2Doc)List, where the columns are lattice points
      * pt, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a point as a column vector
  * Outputs:
      * k, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the maximal such that the
        embedding specified by A is k-jet spanned at pt

Description
===========


degreeOfJetSeparation is a function. Given the set of lattice points of a *note
convex polyhedron: (Polyhedra)Polyhedron, and a point a *note matrix:
(Macaulay2Doc)Matrix, it computes the maximal k such that the associated line
bundle is k-jet spanned at the point
+--------------------------------------+
|i1 : P=convexHull(matrix{{0,2}});     |
+--------------------------------------+
|i2 : Q=convexHull(matrix{{0,4}});     |
+--------------------------------------+
|i3 : A=latticePoints(cayley({P,Q},2));|
+--------------------------------------+
|i4 : pt=matrix{{1},{1}};              |
|                                      |
|              2       1               |
|o4 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                |
+--------------------------------------+
|i5 : degreeOfJetSeparation(A,pt)      |
|                                      |
|o5 = 2                                |
+--------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note isJetSpanned: isJetSpanned, -- checks if the polarized toric variety
    associated to a set of lattice points is k-jet spanned at a given point.

