epsilonBounds -- computes bounds for the Seshadri constant a general point
**************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        epsilonBounds(P)
  * Inputs:
      * P, a *note convex polyhedron: (Polyhedra)Polyhedron,, of dimension 2
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
  * Outputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, Containing bounds a and b such
        that a<=epsilon(X_P,L_P;1_P)<=b

Description
===========


epsilonBounds is a function. It computes bounds for the Seshadri constant at a
general point by applying a set of projections. The integer n determines which
projections are considered.
+---------------------------------------------+
|i1 : P=convexHull(matrix{{0,2}});            |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i2 : Q=convexHull(matrix{{0,4}});            |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i3 : R=cayley({P,Q},2);                      |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i4 : S=convexHull(matrix{{0,1,-1},{1,0,-1}});|
+---------------------------------------------+
|i5 : epsilonBounds(R,10)                     |
|                                             |
|o5 = {2, 2}                                  |
|                                             |
