|i1 : P=randZPoly(5,3)            |
|                                 |
|o1 = P                           |
|                                 |
|o1 : Polyhedron                  |
+---------------------------------+
|i2 : vertices P                  |
|                                 |
|o2 = | -265 -865 -904 -740 -927 ||
|     | -802 -224 113  585  167  ||
|     | -536 -448 -412 330  334  ||
|                                 |
|              3       5          |
|o2 : Matrix QQ  <-- QQ           |
+---------------------------------+

You can also specify an integer e. This has the effect of changing the
randomisation procedure so that a random polytope in [-10^e,10^e]^n is
returned.

+-------------------------------------------+
|i3 : P=randZPoly(5,3,5)                    |
|                                           |
|o3 = P                                     |
|                                           |
|o3 : Polyhedron                            |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i4 : vertices P                            |
|                                           |
|o4 = | 3297   61657  62920  -64604 -92414 ||
|     | -49728 -20276 -40785 45628  14550  ||
|     | -86696 -76074 -66164 -61192 35327  ||
|                                           |
|              3       5                    |
|o4 : Matrix QQ  <-- QQ                     |
+-------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note randQPoly: randQPoly, -- gives a random rational polytope

