toricDiv -- constructs the toric Weil divisor associated to a polytope
**********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        toricDiv(X)
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, of vertices or a *note convex
        polyhedron: (Polyhedra)Polyhedron,.
  * Outputs:
      * a *note toric divisor: (NormalToricVarieties)ToricDivisor,

Description
===========


toricDiv is a function. It returns a *note toric divisor:
(NormalToricVarieties)ToricDivisor, corresponding to a polytope P on the toric
variety associated to the normal fan of P.
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : toricDiv(hypercube(2))                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = D  + D  + D  + D                                                        |
|      0    1    2    3                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : ToricDivisor on normalToricVariety ({{-1, 0}, {1, 0}, {0, -1}, {0, 1}}, |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|{{0, 2}, {0, 3}, {1, 2}, {1, 3}})                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use toricDiv:
=====================

  * "toricDiv(Matrix)"
  * "toricDiv(Polyhedron)"

