torusEmbedding -- gives the toric embedding corresponding to a set of lattice points
************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        torusEmbedding(X)
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, in which the columns are the
        lattice points or a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List, of column vectors
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of monomials giving the
        embedding

Description
===========


torusEmbedding is a function. It takes a set of lattice points as input and
returns a list of monomials giving the corresponding torus embedding.
+--------------------------------------------+
|i1 : torusEmbedding(matrix{{0,1,2},{0,3,4}})|
|                                            |
|            3   2 4                         |
|o1 = {1, x x , x x }                        |
|          0 1   0 1                         |
|                                            |
|o1 : List                                   |
+--------------------------------------------+

